            <ArticleTitle>Pilot trial to determine the efficacy of a low dose of fish oil in the treatment of angina pectoris in the geriatric patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>687-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>23 geriatric patients completed a single-blind placebo controlled, crossover trial using fish oil as adjunctive therapy for stable angina pectoris. The results indicated a significant reduction in the number of anginal attacks, as well as a significant reduction in the consumption of sublingual isosorbide dinitrate tablets. A possible prolonged carry over effect of fish oil was noted after crossover from the active substance to placebo.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
